Kubernetes Interview Question.
Does the container restart when applying/updating the secret object (kubectl apply -f mysecret.yml)? If not, how is the new password applied to the database?

No, the container does not automatically restart when applying or updating the secret object using kubectl apply -f mysecret.yml. To apply the new password to the database without a container restart, you can use mechanisms like environment variable reloading or application-specific mechanisms to pick up the new secret values dynamically without requiring a container restart.
